25,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've noticed that outdoor work and ""comfort"" projects often face significant delays. We should be very careful about what we commit to.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found that we really lack general-purpose rooms, and taking rooms out of service is actually quite expensive because we have to hire outside space!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,George,,"It seems our technicians are burdened with manual tasks that modern equipment should handle, while other staff positions remain empty.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Interestingly, projects that benefit the whole campus are rated much higher than those limited to one area. However, older blocks hide nasty surprises that cause delays.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our budget projections for mechanical plant are outdated, and we've neglected to save for replacing our audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that is worrying. If the costs are rising and we have no reserves, we must choose a project that is truly essential.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, if general rooms are in high demand, maybe we should focus on something everyone can use!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, if we want to avoid delays and help the staff, we should look for something that solves a functional failure rather than just a ""comfort"" upgrade.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, I agree. The data suggests that shared, bookable spaces are the most successful. But we must avoid the older blocks if we want to stay on schedule.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. Given the rising cost of mechanical systems, a complex ventilation project might be a financial trap.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@George, you make a good point. A project based on a necessity, like an inspection finding, is more likely to be finished on time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Does that mean we should avoid the paths? I wonder if they count as ""comfort"" or ""necessity.""","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,George,,The technicians' manual struggle with extraction is a daily burden. Fixing that is a necessity for the staff's wellbeing.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"But @George, if the ventilation upgrade is in an older block, we risk the hazardous material delays I discovered.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,And the tender records suggest mechanical costs are spiking. A ventilation project could easily exceed its budget.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Shizue,,We must balance the needs of the staff with the reality of our timeline and budget.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I still feel strongly that we need more general study space for the students!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,George,,"I understand, but the current inefficiency in the labs is a waste of professional manpower.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"We need a solution that is high-impact, low-risk regarding building materials, and accessible to many.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are weighing the stability of a path network against the utility of a study commons or the necessity of lab upgrades.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
