50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at the options, the Path Network (A) is exposed to weather, which I know causes delays. I am hesitant.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Yumi,,The Central Study Commons (C) sounds perfect! It addresses the shortage of general rooms I found in the booking data.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,George,,The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade (D) is the only one that relieves the technicians from those tedious manual routines.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Option C is in a ground-floor hall. My findings about hazardous materials in older block partitions make me very nervous about that.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B requires AV equipment, for which we have no renewal reserve. Option D is mechanical, and those costs are rising sharply.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"If A is too risky for the calendar and C is risky for the building's interior, perhaps D is the most ""necessary"" despite the cost?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"But @Mizuki, if we don't do C, the students will keep being turned away from rooms!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, if the cost of D is high, can we not justify it by the hours of staff time we save every single week?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, I want to help the students, but a project that stalls for months due to asbestos is a failure for everyone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, logic suggests that while D is necessary, the market volatility for mechanical plant makes it a gamble. Option A's costs are stable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, but the weather! Six weeks lost to rain is a significant slip. I prefer something indoors.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"What about the Media Production Center (B)? It's bookable, which @Mizuki said was a success factor!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,George,,B does nothing for the staff who are already overworked. D is the only choice that provides actual relief.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"B is a specialist room. My data showed specialist rooms are often idle, while general rooms are over capacity. B is not the best use of space.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A fair point, Mizuki. If we seek the most rational choice, we must weigh the stability of A against the utility of C and the necessity of D.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I will vote for the Ventilation Upgrade. It is a necessity, and necessities tend to stay on schedule.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'll stick with the Study Commons. The students really need it, and we can just hope the partitions are clean!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,George,,I must vote for the Ventilation Upgrade. Our staff cannot continue like this.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I cannot support C or D due to the risks of hazardous materials and mechanical costs. I will vote for the Path Network for its stability.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall vote for the Path Network. The tender records show it is the only project where the budget is likely to survive contact with the market.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
